      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, tenure track",
      "description": "Montana State University Northern Employment Opportunities | Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, tenure track Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help MSUN Information About MSUN About Havre Benefits Overview Academics at MSUN Quick Facts University Mission Statement on Diversity Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, tenure track Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In this application, and the required cover letter and list of references, DO NOT include your protected private information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. This does not apply to the Authorization Form for Background Check. Applicants must upload the following with their application: A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your professional and academic career goals, and your interest in the position. A resume or curriculum vitae. A list of three professional references. In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Complete an Authorization Form for Background Check https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation-MSU-Northern.pdf Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing, tenure track Brief Position Overview This is a full-time, tenure track position in Nursing at MSU -Northern. It requires high quality instruction in an ACEN accredited ASN program and in an online Bachelor of Science completion program (RN- BSN ). The ASN courses include lecture, clinical instruction, and lab/simulation instruction completed in a face-to-face format. The online RN- BSN completion program requires nursing instruction through distance learning. Applicants with specialties across all areas of nursing are encouraged to apply. MSUN will only consider applicants who are authorized to work in the US and will not sponsor applicants for work visas. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant or Associate Professor Position Number TBD Department Nursing Division College of Health Sciences Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Exempt Union Affiliation Montana Federation of Public Employees FTE 1 Benefits Eligible Yes Compensation Annual Salary Commensurate with credentials and experience and within the guidelines set by the collective bargaining agreement. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement This is a full-time, tenure track position in Nursing at MSU -Northern. It requires high quality instruction in an ACEN accredited ASN program and in an online Bachelor of Science completion program (RN- BSN ). The ASN courses include lecture, clinical instruction, and lab/simulation instruction completed in a face-to-face format. The online RN- BSN completion program requires nursing instruction through distance learning. Applicants with specialties across all areas of nursing are encouraged to apply. Duties and Responsibilities • Develop, implement, and evaluate high-quality courses in an Associate of Science ( ASN ) program and an Online RN- BSN Completion program • Establish and maintain strong relationships with clinical affiliates • Provide lecture and lab/clinical instruction in area of specialty • Provide instruction in Simulation Lab • Advise nursing and pre-nursing students • Participate in the ongoing development and evaluation of program outcomes and program effectiveness for accrediting bodies • Serve on college and university-level committees and engage in campus activities • Contribute to the development and evaluation of student admission, progression, retention, and graduation policies of the program • Demonstrate scholarly activity by continued professional development and active participation in professional organizations Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills • Holds a Master’s degree in Nursing ( MSN ) from a nationally accredited program; OR • Holds a Bachelor’s degree in Nursing ( BSN ) and currently enrolled in an MSN program with a completion timeline of no more than 5 years. • Maintains a current, unencumbered Montana Registered Nursing license or Compact state licensure and/or is eligible for RN licensure in the State of Montana • Possesses significant nursing experience in a clinical setting as a registered nurse. • Demonstrates excellent communication skills, along with a high level of initiative, competency in critical thinking, and sound clinical judgement. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Teaching experience in an ASN or BSN program Experience in distance education including web-based course development and implementation Experience with Simulation Lab instruction Demonstrated potential to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students Demonstrated a commitment to supporting the mission of the college and university Has successfully completed a Doctor of Nursing Practice ( DNP ) program The Successful Candidate Will Special Requirements Physical Demands Typical office, classroom, and lab environments. The Program The Department The College This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 2700002P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date January 1, 2027 or sooner Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Until an adequate pool is established No Special Instructions Summary In this application, and the required cover letter and list of references, DO NOT include your protected private information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. This does not apply to the Authorization Form for Background Check. Applicants must upload the following with their application: A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your professional and academic career goals, and your interest in the position. A resume or curriculum vitae. A list of three professional references. In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Complete an Authorization Form for Background Check https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation- MSU -Northern.pdf Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.msun.edu/postings/2697 EEOC Statement Montana State University-Northern ( MSUN ) is an equal opportunity employer. MSUN does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSUN provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Director of Human Resources /Title IX Montana State University-Northern 300 11th Street West Havre, MT 59501 E-mail: rebecca.farr@msun.edu Location: 208 Cowan Hall Tel: (406) 265.3568 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Transcript Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Send your completed Authorization for Background Check form to the Human Resources Department. Access the form at this link, https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation-MSU-Northern.pdf In the application field for Background Check, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. (Open Ended Question) © Montana State University Northern Accessibility Admissions Administration Contact List Jobs Privacy Policy Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
